        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Clarify BCE and eraYear usage for Gregorian calendar in Temporal docs]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/39973</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/39973"/>
        <updated>2025-06-18T03:48:21.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12285999?u=183d27a6aca0718cb83ecec3c8e7745502384f48&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Replaces the incorrect statement <code class="notranslate">{ era: "bce", eraYear: 1 }</code> for year <code class="notranslate">-1</code> with the accurate <code class="notranslate">{ era: "bce", eraYear: 2 }</code>, based on astronomical year numbering.<br>
Also removes outdated phrasing ("skips year 0") and avoids internal implementation terms like <code class="notranslate">"gregory-inverse"</code>.</p>
<p dir="auto">This aligns with the suggestion from <a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/Josh-Cena/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/Josh-Cena">@Josh-Cena</a> and confirmation from <a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/joeljpresent/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/joeljpresent">@joeljpresent</a> in issue <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3144065488" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/39936" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/39936/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/39936">#39936</a>.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">To provide accurate and culturally understandable information about how the Temporal API represents BCE dates using <code class="notranslate">era</code> and <code class="notranslate">eraYear</code>, and to correct the previous misleading example.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Removed incorrect phrasing about astronomical year numbering.</li>
<li>Omitted technical output notes (e.g., <code class="notranslate">"gregory-inverse"</code>) for clarity, as suggested.</li>
<li>Followed MDN’s reader-first guidance while remaining technically accurate.</li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #39936.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3144065488" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/39936" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/39936/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/39936">#39936</a></p>]]></content>
